@format 1
@id section-naming.inline-editor-input
@title Edit inline section name fields
@section Section naming
@area In Split tab
@entry normal-text,comma-input,enter-key,escape-key,field-focus-lost
@summary Handle buffered text, comma field-stepping, explicit commit/cancel, and deferred focus-loss commit while the Split Sections-panel inline editor is active.
@related section-naming.inline-editor-open, section-naming.pending-inline-commit, section-naming.switch-inline-edit-target, section-naming.common.apply-name-state
@tag section
@tag split
@tag name
@tag rename
@tag inline-editor

@alias panel = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PSection

[normal-text] Ordinary inline text entry <input>
~ This starts with ordinary inline text entry.
[Technical explanation]
= Normal text editing changes only the TextBox buffer until a commit-triggering event occurs.
> buffered

[comma-input] PreviewTextInput comma <input>
~ This starts when the user types a comma in the inline name editor.
[Technical explanation]
- PSectionStepAttach consumes comma input; the main name steps to prefix and prefix steps to suffix by revealing/focusing/selecting the next field @ panel.PSectionStepAttach(...)
> comma-check

[enter-key] Name/prefix/suffix Enter <input>
~ This starts when the user presses Enter in a naming field.
[Technical explanation]
- Enter in any inline field calls PSectionEditCommit and marks the key handled @ panel.PSectionFieldBuild(...) / KeyDown Enter
> enter-commit

[escape-key] Name/prefix/suffix Escape <input>
~ This starts when the user presses Escape in a naming field.
[Technical explanation]
- Escape calls PSectionEditCancel and marks the key handled @ panel.PSectionFieldBuild(...) / KeyDown Escape
> cancel

[field-focus-lost] Name/prefix/suffix LostFocus <input>
~ This starts when focus leaves one of the naming fields.
[Technical explanation]
- LostFocus calls PSectionEditClose; unless the panel is rebuilding, it schedules the focus decision at DispatcherPriority.Input @ panel.PSectionEditClose(...)
> deferred-focus-check

[buffered] Pending inline name text <output>
~ This path ends with pending inline name text.
[Technical explanation]
= Stored LPiece name fields remain unchanged.

[comma-check] Next field exists <decision>
~ The program checks next field exists.
[Technical explanation]
- PSectionStepAttach always handles the comma; suffix comma is consumed even though there is no next field @ panel.PSectionStepAttach(...)
? "Next field exists" > stepped
? "Suffix has no next field" > suffix-comma

[enter-commit] Explicit commit requested <process>
~ The user confirms the edited section name.
[Technical explanation]
- PSectionEditCommit trims the three buffers and calls PFlowNameSet @ panel.PSectionEditCommit(...)
> map:section-naming.common.apply-name-state

[cancel] Discard inline buffers <output>
~ The unconfirmed inline name text is discarded.
[Technical explanation]
- PSectionEditCancel clears the editing index and TextBox references, then rebuilds from stored section state without calling PFlowNameSet @ panel.PSectionEditCancel(...)

[deferred-focus-check] Focus after dispatcher turn <decision>
~ The program checks focus after UI queue turn.
[Technical explanation]
- PSectionEditClose returns while rebuilding or while PSectionFocusCheck finds keyboard focus in any of the three editor fields; otherwise it calls PSectionEditCommit @ panel.PSectionEditClose(...)
@ panel.PSectionFocusCheck(...)
? "Focus remains inside editor or rebuild active" > keep-editing
? "Focus left all editor fields" > focus-commit

[stepped] Continue editing next field <output>
~ This path ends with continue editing next field.
[Technical explanation]
= No commit occurs.

[suffix-comma] Suffix comma consumed <output>
~ This path ends with suffix comma consumed.
[Technical explanation]
= The comma is not inserted and no commit occurs.

[keep-editing] Keep inline editor open <output>
~ This path ends with keep inline editor open.
[Technical explanation]
= Moving focus among the three naming fields does not commit.

[focus-commit] Deferred commit requested <process>
~ After focus leaves the editor, the program confirms the edited section name.
[Technical explanation]
- PSectionEditClose calls PSectionEditCommit after focus has left all editor fields @ panel.PSectionEditCommit(...)
> map:section-naming.common.apply-name-state
